  "problem": "A saline reservoir for a medical research lab can hold up to $160\\,\\text{gal}$ of solution. Initially, it contains $100\\,\\text{gal}$ of saline solution with $25\\,\\text{lb}$ of dissolved salt. A more concentrated saline solution with concentration $1.0\\,\\text{lb/gal}$ flows into the reservoir at a rate of $6\\,\\text{gal/min},$ while the completely mixed solution drains out at a rate of $4\\,\\text{gal/min}.$ Rounded to one decimal place, find the amount of salt in the reservoir at the moment it begins to overflow.",
